1
00:00:09,380 --> 00:00:10,620
(Lee Min Jung)

2
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:15,420
(Kim Ji Seok)

3
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:24,860
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

4
00:00:24,930 --> 00:00:26,330
(All child actor scenes were filmed with a guardian present...)

5
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:27,770
(with professional staff and in accordance with safety guidelines.)

6
00:00:28,470 --> 00:00:29,570
Won Ho.

7
00:00:29,570 --> 00:00:31,040
Won Ho, can we talk for a minute?

8
00:00:31,570 --> 00:00:32,570
Won Ho.

9
00:00:33,610 --> 00:00:34,610
Move.

10
00:00:35,140 --> 00:00:36,170
Wait, hold on.

11
00:00:37,610 --> 00:00:38,680
Right now,

12
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:40,250
our employees and the production crew...

13
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:43,520
are all waiting for you. If you say you're not doing it now,

14
00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:45,150
what about all the production costs?

15
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:48,520
Then what about me? I'm so furious that you tricked me...

16
00:00:48,590 --> 00:00:50,460
that I can't do this show or anything else.

17
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:52,120
What about me? What am I supposed to do?

18
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:54,860
Fine, it was all my fault.

19
00:00:54,860 --> 00:00:55,890
I'm so sorry.

20
00:00:56,090 --> 00:00:58,000
I tricked you and made a fool out of you.

21
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,470
That's all my fault. So please, just this once, okay?

22
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:02,770
No.

23
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:05,600
Not for me, for our shop.

24
00:01:05,670 --> 00:01:07,910
Stop using the shop as an excuse. This is all about your greed.

25
00:01:08,010 --> 00:01:10,480
This all happened because you were greedy.

26
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:13,550
So...

27
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:16,450
you refuse to do it, no matter what?

28
00:01:16,710 --> 00:01:18,020
Yes. Move.

29
00:01:22,790 --> 00:01:23,820
Wait.

30
00:01:25,060 --> 00:01:26,360
I'm not done talking.

31
00:01:26,930 --> 00:01:27,930
What now?

32
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:30,760
Fine.

33
00:01:31,730 --> 00:01:32,960
I've made my decision.

34
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:38,040
What was that?

35
00:01:41,540 --> 00:01:42,540
Let's get...

36
00:01:44,580 --> 00:01:46,640
What are you saying? Speak up, I can't hear you.

37
00:02:03,130 --> 00:02:04,830
What did you just do?

38
00:02:07,270 --> 00:02:08,430
Hey, Baek Mi Young.

39
00:02:10,370 --> 00:02:11,370
I mean...

40
00:02:21,450 --> 00:02:23,480
At first, I had no idea what it was.

41
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:27,320
She suddenly pulled something off her finger and threw it.

42
00:02:28,190 --> 00:02:31,160
I thought, "No way. She has to be joking."

43
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:35,090
It was a real Cartier.

44
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:37,460
If it was a real Cartier...

45
00:02:39,130 --> 00:02:40,300
Doesn't that mean she wants a divorce?

46
00:02:40,470 --> 00:02:43,870
Exactly. She's the one who's in the wrong, not me. So why?

47
00:02:47,210 --> 00:02:48,910
What is this? I didn't order it.

48
00:02:49,070 --> 00:02:51,080
It's from the person over there.

49
00:02:57,420 --> 00:02:59,150
She looks pretty young, doesn't she?

50
00:03:02,950 --> 00:03:03,960
No, thank you.

51
00:03:05,490 --> 00:03:07,130
Please tell them we appreciate it, but we have to decline.

52
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:09,490
We're in the middle of a serious conversation.

53
00:03:09,890 --> 00:03:11,330
Yes, I understand.

54
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:20,670
Regardless of who's at fault, if she really asks for a divorce...

55
00:03:21,540 --> 00:03:22,770
What are you going to do then?

56
00:03:23,270 --> 00:03:25,040
Well, then I guess we'll have to.

57
00:03:25,380 --> 00:03:26,380
Really?

58
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:28,180
You'd actually get a divorce?

59
00:03:28,350 --> 00:03:29,650
Goodness.

60
00:03:30,380 --> 00:03:31,620
That Cartier ring... Darn it.

61
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:34,690
It was a limited edition.

62
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:03,180
Hey, are you asleep?

63
00:04:03,950 --> 00:04:05,320
If you're awake, we need to talk.

64
00:04:38,050 --> 00:04:39,050
Wait.

65
00:04:40,790 --> 00:04:42,050
I'm not done talking.

66
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:43,960
What now?

67
00:04:46,060 --> 00:04:49,330
Fine. I've made my decision.

68
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:52,430
Let's get a divorce.

69
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:54,100
What was that?

70
00:04:54,830 --> 00:04:55,830
Let's get a divorce.

71
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:58,900
I said, let's get a divorce. Let's do it.

72
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:02,710
What are you saying? Speak up, I can't hear you.

73
00:05:14,020 --> 00:05:15,790
What did you just do?

74
00:05:44,550 --> 00:05:46,220
Hi, everyone.

75
00:05:46,520 --> 00:05:47,750
Hello.

76
00:05:48,190 --> 00:05:49,950
I know you're all curious about what happened...

77
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:51,390
after we filmed the show yesterday.

78
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:55,960
To be honest, my husband and I tried really hard.

79
00:05:56,460 --> 00:05:58,100
But right before the shoot,

80
00:05:58,160 --> 00:06:00,730
I came down with a terrible stomach bug,

81
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:03,630
so filming has been postponed indefinitely.

82
00:06:03,940 --> 00:06:05,040
It's such a shame, isn't it?

83
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:07,470
I'm upset, but what can I do?

84
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:09,070
It's all my fault.

85
00:06:09,540 --> 00:06:11,880
I should have taken better care of myself.

86
00:06:13,410 --> 00:06:16,150
Thank you all so much for your concern.

87
00:06:16,610 --> 00:06:18,450
Tomorrow, I'll be introducing...

88
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:20,990
this year's new Fall-Winter dress line,

89
00:06:21,050 --> 00:06:22,350
and I'll be back to see you all again.

90
00:06:22,520 --> 00:06:24,120
Yes, I'll see you tomorrow.

91
00:06:24,660 --> 00:06:25,690
Bye.

92
00:06:35,270 --> 00:06:36,870
We need to talk.

93
00:06:37,740 --> 00:06:38,740
About what?

94
00:06:39,070 --> 00:06:40,840
Why did you throw your ring yesterday?

95
00:06:41,340 --> 00:06:43,510
Why? Because I don't need it anymore.

96
00:06:44,310 --> 00:06:45,310
What?

97
00:06:45,380 --> 00:06:46,940
I told you clearly yesterday.

98
00:06:47,410 --> 00:06:48,410
I want a divorce.

99
00:06:51,180 --> 00:06:52,950
Baek Mi Young, get over here right now.

100
00:06:53,020 --> 00:06:54,890
Come here. Let's sit down and talk first. Okay?

101
00:06:55,020 --> 00:06:56,150
Forget it. I don't have time.

102
00:06:56,320 --> 00:06:57,360
But...

103
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:03,090
Darn it...

104
00:07:15,110 --> 00:07:19,740
I was hoping the show would help the company get back on its feet.

105
00:07:20,710 --> 00:07:22,410
It's a real shame.

106
00:07:22,750 --> 00:07:24,150
It's a shame, but there's nothing we can do.

107
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:26,120
We just have to keep doing our jobs.

108
00:07:27,450 --> 00:07:28,520
Isn't that right, CEO Ji?

109
00:07:28,820 --> 00:07:31,790
Being on TV wasn't a good fit for us anyway.

110
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:36,590
But we can barely make payroll next month as it is.

111
00:07:38,330 --> 00:07:40,030
Is that CEO Ji's fault?

112
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:43,270
It's not like CEO Ji is refusing to pay the employees.

113
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:44,940
No, what I mean is...

114
00:07:47,540 --> 00:07:48,770
Then what about CEO Baek?

115
00:07:49,170 --> 00:07:51,580
Do you think CEO Baek refused to pay everyone,

116
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:53,210
and that's why she's trying so hard all by herself?

117
00:07:54,110 --> 00:07:55,280
What do you mean, all by herself?

118
00:07:56,110 --> 00:07:58,380
CEO Ji is doing his best too.

119
00:07:59,220 --> 00:08:00,920
Does someone doing their best...

120
00:08:00,990 --> 00:08:03,250
just blow a huge opportunity and run off?

121
00:08:03,420 --> 00:08:04,490
What do you mean, "run off?"

122
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:05,890
There will be other opportunities.

123
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:08,330
Director Song, you're speaking way out of line.

124
00:08:09,490 --> 00:08:11,360
Are you pointing at me?

125
00:08:12,660 --> 00:08:14,230
You're going to hit someone if you keep that up.

126
00:08:14,430 --> 00:08:16,230
Seriously, who do you think you're pointing at?

127
00:08:16,300 --> 00:08:18,140
- Unbelievable. - What are you two doing in here?

128
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:19,870
- I'm right, aren't I? - Seriously, stop it.

129
00:08:19,940 --> 00:08:21,940
CEO Ji.

130
00:08:23,940 --> 00:08:26,780
Yeong Yu, don't you know how to knock?

131
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:28,180
I'm sorry.

132
00:08:28,410 --> 00:08:31,920
Excuse me, CEO Ji, but I think you'll want to take this call.

133
00:08:32,820 --> 00:08:33,820
For me?

134
00:08:36,450 --> 00:08:39,620
Yes. When did you have in mind?

135
00:08:41,430 --> 00:08:42,490
Yes, that's possible.

136
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:45,230
Did you have something in mind?

137
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:49,370
So the person CEO Ji is on the phone with right now...

138
00:08:49,470 --> 00:08:50,800
is really Cheon Man Ju?

139
00:08:51,070 --> 00:08:52,200
Apparently so.

140
00:08:53,670 --> 00:08:56,340
I'm dying to know why Cheon Man Ju called.

141
00:08:56,410 --> 00:08:58,110
Yes, I understand. Okay.

142
00:09:01,150 --> 00:09:02,310
What did Cheon Man Ju say?

143
00:09:02,710 --> 00:09:05,120
She said she's coming here later for a dress consultation.

144
00:09:07,050 --> 00:09:09,820
- Is it really Cheon Man Ju? - The ultimate icon for Gen Z.

145
00:09:10,150 --> 00:09:12,490
- A celebrity's celebrity. - Is this for real?

146
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:15,960
Cheon Man Ju is really coming here herself?

147
00:09:16,160 --> 00:09:19,300
- Yes. - Someone famous is coming here?

148
00:09:20,460 --> 00:09:21,670
Did you hear that right?

149
00:09:21,830 --> 00:09:23,230
Was it really Cheon Man Ju?

150
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:25,240
What, am I deaf? How could I mishear that?

151
00:09:25,300 --> 00:09:26,670
I told you it was Cheon Man Ju.

152
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:29,170
- Incredible. - This is incredible.

153
00:09:29,870 --> 00:09:32,480
- Cheon Man Ju, for real? - Amazing.

154
00:09:32,540 --> 00:09:33,540
This is huge.

155
00:09:33,810 --> 00:09:35,180
Have you ever seen Cheon Man Ju in person?

156
00:09:36,410 --> 00:09:38,350
So, wait, who is Cheon Man Ju?

157
00:09:43,890 --> 00:09:46,290
- Why? - This is a one-time opportunity.

158
00:09:46,820 --> 00:09:50,030
From now on, just use Cheon Man Ju as an excuse with Mi Young.

159
00:09:50,860 --> 00:09:53,630
- What? - Cheon Man Ju, for a dress fitting,

160
00:09:53,860 --> 00:09:56,070
and what's more important to J&White than her right now?

161
00:09:57,170 --> 00:09:58,170
The divorce?

162
00:09:58,240 --> 00:09:59,400
Is that more important than Cheon Man Ju?

163
00:09:59,740 --> 00:10:00,740
Than the company?

164
00:10:01,210 --> 00:10:04,640
- Of course not. - Exactly.

165
00:10:05,280 --> 00:10:06,440
For the time being, you need to think...

166
00:10:06,510 --> 00:10:07,510
only about Cheon Man Ju.

167
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:10,010
At least until her wedding is over.

168
00:10:15,220 --> 00:10:16,890
You know who Cheon Man Ju is, right?

169
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:19,990
Of course you do.

170
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:22,960
Anyone in this country who doesn't know her must be a spy.

171
00:10:23,630 --> 00:10:25,600
Then you must have been a spy until this morning.

172
00:10:27,730 --> 00:10:30,970
Anyway, for Cheon Man Ju's sake,

173
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:34,210
let's put this talk about our divorce on hold.

174
00:10:34,570 --> 00:10:36,710
What does Cheon Man Ju have to do with our divorce?

175
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:38,710
Of course it has something to do with it.

176
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:41,080
Look, imagine you're Cheon Man Ju.

177
00:10:41,410 --> 00:10:44,650
You come here for the one dress you'll wear in your lifetime,

178
00:10:44,780 --> 00:10:45,780
and what do you find?

179
00:10:45,780 --> 00:10:47,590
The owners are in the middle of a divorce.

180
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:49,350
They're fighting over whether to get divorced or not.

181
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:52,420
How about it? Isn't that kind of a turn-off?

182
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:54,190
Don't you think that's bad luck?

183
00:10:57,430 --> 00:10:59,460
Mi Young, this is a golden opportunity...

184
00:10:59,530 --> 00:11:00,700
to save the company.

185
00:11:00,770 --> 00:11:03,000
We still have to pay our employees next month.

186
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:11,280
Cheon Man Ju is here.

187
00:11:27,430 --> 00:11:29,490
- I hope you had an easy trip over. - Hello.

188
00:11:30,590 --> 00:11:32,260
Hello. I'm Cheon Man Ju.

189
00:11:34,300 --> 00:11:37,200
A star doesn't drive herself, so that's not an issue.

190
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,810
It's a bit smaller than I expected.

191
00:11:44,410 --> 00:11:45,410
It's my first time.

192
00:11:51,980 --> 00:11:53,050
Did you see Cheon Man Ju?

193
00:11:54,120 --> 00:11:55,150
I did.

194
00:11:55,520 --> 00:11:56,550
What's she like in person?

195
00:11:57,120 --> 00:11:58,120
How should I put it?

196
00:11:58,490 --> 00:12:01,960
Even as a woman, I have to say she has an extraordinary aura.

197
00:12:02,190 --> 00:12:03,690
Gosh, of course.

198
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:05,800
The man she's marrying...

199
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:08,170
is one lucky guy.

200
00:12:08,470 --> 00:12:09,470
Goodness.

201
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:12,300
She had this bag with a jewel on it this big,

202
00:12:12,370 --> 00:12:14,640
- and she was holding it like this. - Really? Incredible.

203
00:12:14,710 --> 00:12:15,970
- And... - Excuse me.

204
00:12:16,610 --> 00:12:20,850
I'm with Cheon Man Ju. Do you happen to know where she is?

205
00:12:21,750 --> 00:12:23,650
Yes, please follow me.

206
00:12:23,710 --> 00:12:24,720
This way.

207
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:31,360
She looks familiar.

208
00:12:32,260 --> 00:12:33,420
She's my personal photographer.

209
00:12:34,790 --> 00:12:35,860
Hello.

210
00:12:35,930 --> 00:12:37,630
My name is Ahn Hee Ju.

211
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:39,660
- Yes. - She'll be handling everything...

212
00:12:39,660 --> 00:12:41,570
related to the photography.

213
00:12:41,870 --> 00:12:43,900
I'm a bit particular about my photos,

214
00:12:44,070 --> 00:12:45,640
so I can't just entrust them to anyone.

215
00:12:47,640 --> 00:12:51,010
- These are our sample dresses. - I...

216
00:12:51,610 --> 00:12:53,410
I'm a really big fan of yours, CEO Ji.

217
00:12:54,510 --> 00:12:57,210
I fell completely in love when I saw your dresses.

218
00:12:57,450 --> 00:12:59,980
The dresses are so my style.

219
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:02,120
Thank you.

220
00:13:02,890 --> 00:13:05,720
This is from the J&White signature line...

221
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:08,290
You see,

222
00:13:08,760 --> 00:13:11,530
I have this huge fantasy about my wedding dress.

223
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:15,470
A Dress of a Lifetime that's perfect for me.

224
00:13:16,170 --> 00:13:17,230
That's possible, right?

225
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:18,770
Of course. It's possible.

226
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:20,700
A perfectly fitting Dress of a Lifetime.

227
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:25,080
Look at that confidence.

228
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:27,180
I definitely came to the right place.

229
00:13:28,080 --> 00:13:29,150
Hee Ju.

230
00:13:29,250 --> 00:13:31,120
I think I'll get my party dress here too.

231
00:13:32,120 --> 00:13:33,550
You're having a party too?

232
00:13:33,820 --> 00:13:36,290
It's before the wedding, so of course.

233
00:13:39,060 --> 00:13:41,530
It's in the suite at the Calvin Hotel.

234
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:45,230
Oh, I'm so sorry.

235
00:13:46,260 --> 00:13:47,330
It's okay.

236
00:13:56,610 --> 00:14:00,180
(CEO Calvin Kim)

237
00:14:04,620 --> 00:14:06,350
Contract with J&White is finalised.

238
00:14:06,850 --> 00:14:09,890
So now all that's left is to deliver the invitation, right, Calvin?

239
00:14:10,150 --> 00:14:12,020
(Cheon Man Ju)

240
00:14:21,130 --> 00:14:23,070
Okay, this is our fitting room.

241
00:14:23,230 --> 00:14:25,540
Feel free to try anything on, and just let me know.

242
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:28,040
I'm already so excited.

243
00:14:33,780 --> 00:14:34,780
Yes.

244
00:14:39,350 --> 00:14:40,350
Excuse me.

245
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:42,520
Have we met somewhere before?

246
00:14:42,990 --> 00:14:45,990
- What? - You just look familiar.

247
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:47,360
Oh, really?

248
00:14:47,630 --> 00:14:49,160
Right? Where have I seen you?

249
00:14:49,460 --> 00:14:50,730
So you do remember.

250
00:14:51,460 --> 00:14:53,660
By the way, did you turn me down on purpose yesterday?

251
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:55,200
Yesterday?

252
00:14:55,970 --> 00:14:57,100
You don't remember?

253
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:58,200
The cocktail.

254
00:14:58,470 --> 00:14:59,500
Cocktail?

255
00:15:05,480 --> 00:15:07,110
What is this? I didn't order it.

256
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:09,450
It's from the person over there.

257
00:15:14,180 --> 00:15:15,550
Right.

258
00:15:16,350 --> 00:15:18,020
But do you know me?

259
00:15:18,420 --> 00:15:21,660
- What? - Why send me a cocktail...

260
00:15:25,760 --> 00:15:27,400
Think carefully.

261
00:15:27,770 --> 00:15:28,970
The restroom is that way, right?

262
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:48,720
Man Ju.

263
00:15:48,950 --> 00:15:51,290
You're much slimmer than I expected.

264
00:15:51,460 --> 00:15:53,560
Is that an insult or a compliment?

265
00:15:56,090 --> 00:15:58,300
Don't you think my stomach is sticking out a little?

266
00:15:58,860 --> 00:16:01,200
Your stomach? What are you talking about?

267
00:16:01,400 --> 00:16:02,970
You're so slim.

268
00:16:03,030 --> 00:16:05,100
I'm five months pregnant.

269
00:16:05,900 --> 00:16:08,770
It should look a little different from a regular potbelly.

270
00:16:09,310 --> 00:16:10,540
You've never been pregnant, have you?

271
00:16:14,550 --> 00:16:15,750
So you've never been pregnant.

272
00:16:19,450 --> 00:16:22,150
Congratulations on your pregnancy.

273
00:16:22,520 --> 00:16:23,550
But...

274
00:16:24,150 --> 00:16:25,590
if you're pregnant,

275
00:16:26,190 --> 00:16:28,160
instead of a dress with this silhouette,

276
00:16:28,390 --> 00:16:31,460
how about a bell-line dress that falls from here?

277
00:16:31,660 --> 00:16:32,800
- What did you say? - It'd be a different story...

278
00:16:32,800 --> 00:16:33,900
if you were in the first trimester,

279
00:16:33,960 --> 00:16:35,730
but at this stage,

280
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:38,340
an A-line dress is too tight and could be dangerous.

281
00:16:38,740 --> 00:16:40,540
And as it happens, this season's trend...

282
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:43,040
is the bell-line dress as well.

283
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:46,210
Make it an A-line, no exceptions.

284
00:16:48,450 --> 00:16:51,650
- What? - I'll worry about my own stomach.

285
00:16:52,180 --> 00:16:54,590
Just make the waist tight.

286
00:16:55,050 --> 00:16:56,690
Man Ju, I really can't...

287
00:16:58,120 --> 00:17:00,090
You don't like my belly?

288
00:17:02,890 --> 00:17:03,960
Whatever.

289
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:05,330
Just do exactly as I say.

290
00:17:06,030 --> 00:17:08,500
You just care about getting paid anyway, right?

291
00:17:10,130 --> 00:17:11,800
I shouldn't have told you I was pregnant.

292
00:17:13,100 --> 00:17:14,340
My pregnancy is a secret.

293
00:17:14,710 --> 00:17:16,270
Yes, of course.

294
00:17:17,370 --> 00:17:19,140
An A-line dress like this is out of the question.

295
00:17:19,510 --> 00:17:20,910
Revise the dress design.

296
00:17:21,450 --> 00:17:23,210
The waist on this is too tight.

297
00:17:23,610 --> 00:17:25,380
Let's go with a bell-line dress with a more comfortable fit.

298
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:28,220
Why? Didn't you say Cheon Man Ju wanted this one?

299
00:17:28,420 --> 00:17:30,190
And you still think so after seeing her?

300
00:17:30,550 --> 00:17:32,990
This design isn't flattering for her figure at all.

301
00:17:33,090 --> 00:17:36,890
But a bell-line dress has puffs, so it can cover up her flaws.

302
00:17:36,960 --> 00:17:38,900
That's not our call to make.

303
00:17:39,030 --> 00:17:40,500
Our job is to make the dress the client wants...

304
00:17:40,560 --> 00:17:42,630
and make sure they're satisfied.

305
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:45,270
Then let's just revise the waistline to be a little higher.

306
00:17:45,340 --> 00:17:46,940
Why are you acting like such an amateur?

307
00:17:47,700 --> 00:17:48,710
Be honest with me.

308
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:50,310
Is it because Cheon Man Ju disrespected you earlier...

309
00:17:50,370 --> 00:17:51,380
that you're pulling a power trip?

310
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:52,810
Do you really think I'm on a power trip...

311
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:53,880
with Cheon Man Ju right now?

312
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:56,010
If this isn't a power trip, what is it?

313
00:17:56,310 --> 00:17:57,480
Didn't you say yourself...

314
00:17:57,550 --> 00:17:58,880
that the client's needs are the top priority?

315
00:17:59,420 --> 00:18:02,550
It's because I made a mistake with Cheon Man Ju.

316
00:18:03,050 --> 00:18:05,420
- A mistake? - Yes, in the fitting room.

317
00:18:06,220 --> 00:18:08,490
I think she chose this dress rashly because of it.

318
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:10,760
She's going to regret it later.

319
00:18:10,960 --> 00:18:12,530
She won't regret it at all.

320
00:18:12,860 --> 00:18:15,230
Once she sees the dress I made, she'll love it.

321
00:18:15,630 --> 00:18:16,970
Leave the dress to me.

322
00:18:17,070 --> 00:18:19,040
This is a matter of my pride and philosophy.

323
00:18:19,570 --> 00:18:20,570
So,

324
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:22,770
you refuse to change the design no matter what, is that it?

325
00:18:22,970 --> 00:18:24,880
I'm absolutely not changing it.

326
00:18:25,180 --> 00:18:27,640
Not without a request from Man Ju. Not even if the sky falls.

327
00:18:32,380 --> 00:18:33,420
Then,

328
00:18:33,720 --> 00:18:35,650
do a corset fitting instead of a zipper fitting.

329
00:18:35,750 --> 00:18:36,750
You can do that, can't you?

330
00:18:36,820 --> 00:18:38,360
What's with you?

331
00:18:38,490 --> 00:18:41,090
Since Man Ju will probably gain more weight,

332
00:18:41,360 --> 00:18:42,860
do a corset fitting.

333
00:18:42,930 --> 00:18:44,730
How would you know if Man Ju is going to...

334
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:46,400
gain weight or not?

335
00:18:46,530 --> 00:18:47,830
I just know.

336
00:18:48,170 --> 00:18:50,330
Man Ju will gain weight even if the sky falls.

337
00:18:50,730 --> 00:18:52,740
So do a corset fitting, understand?

338
00:18:53,740 --> 00:18:54,840
Darn it.

339
00:19:03,810 --> 00:19:05,880
(Punghae Turtle Shrine, Turtle Master)

340
00:19:08,020 --> 00:19:10,120
I pray.

341
00:19:10,450 --> 00:19:13,160
Oh, great spirits, I pray.

342
00:19:16,990 --> 00:19:18,200
Your fate lies across the water.

343
00:19:18,260 --> 00:19:19,400
My gosh.

344
00:19:19,760 --> 00:19:21,130
Yes, that's right.

345
00:19:21,700 --> 00:19:23,200
My son studied abroad.

346
00:19:23,270 --> 00:19:25,570
He went to Milan, Italy, to study fashion.

347
00:19:25,940 --> 00:19:27,800
You're as amazing as they say.

348
00:19:28,340 --> 00:19:30,310
So, what is it you want to ask?

349
00:19:30,540 --> 00:19:33,640
About a baby. My second son's wife.

350
00:19:33,910 --> 00:19:35,910
I want to know when she can have a baby.

351
00:19:37,780 --> 00:19:39,020
All right.

352
00:19:40,720 --> 00:19:42,120
Let's see if a baby is in her future.

353
00:19:52,130 --> 00:19:53,130
It's over.

354
00:19:53,430 --> 00:19:54,570
It has been for a long time.

355
00:19:54,870 --> 00:19:55,870
What?

356
00:19:58,470 --> 00:20:00,500
They were a bad match, blocking each other's fortunes...

357
00:20:00,570 --> 00:20:01,840
and twisting their fates.

358
00:20:03,340 --> 00:20:04,780
They're destined to separate soon.

359
00:20:05,540 --> 00:20:07,510
No, we can't have Won Ho getting a divorce too.

360
00:20:07,580 --> 00:20:10,750
Master, please, take a closer look.

361
00:20:11,520 --> 00:20:13,120
There's no need to look further.

362
00:20:13,320 --> 00:20:15,950
This is all because of your son.

363
00:20:16,090 --> 00:20:19,620
- What about my son? - He committed an unforgivable sin.

364
00:20:19,660 --> 00:20:20,760
That's not true.

365
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:23,060
My little brother wouldn't hurt a fly.

366
00:20:23,190 --> 00:20:26,100
But his wife isn't exactly blameless either.

367
00:20:26,230 --> 00:20:27,430
Exactly.

368
00:20:27,500 --> 00:20:29,670
Stop beating around the bush...

369
00:20:29,730 --> 00:20:32,640
and tell us straight.

370
00:20:33,140 --> 00:20:34,140
Fine.

371
00:20:35,940 --> 00:20:37,270
Let's see.

372
00:20:37,870 --> 00:20:39,980
Let's take a good, clear look.

373
00:20:54,690 --> 00:20:56,390
Who killed someone?

374
00:20:57,430 --> 00:20:58,660
What did you say?

375
00:20:58,960 --> 00:21:00,430
What? Who killed someone?

376
00:21:01,230 --> 00:21:03,500
Mom, let's go. I think we've seen enough.

377
00:21:03,570 --> 00:21:05,800
- This is ridiculous. - What is this?

378
00:21:05,870 --> 00:21:07,840
Hey. Pay up before you go, you punk.

379
00:21:07,900 --> 00:21:08,970
What? You're calling me a punk?

380
00:21:09,840 --> 00:21:13,480
- Here. Take it, you punk. Let's go. - He's a complete fraud.

381
00:21:13,680 --> 00:21:14,780
"Turtle Master," my foot.

382
00:21:14,850 --> 00:21:16,910
I hope you turn into turtle soup when you die.

383
00:21:20,120 --> 00:21:21,220
- Where did he go? - There.

384
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:25,660
- Where are you going? Come out. - There.

385
00:21:25,720 --> 00:21:27,060
Come out.

386
00:21:27,120 --> 00:21:28,130
Hey.

387
00:21:28,190 --> 00:21:29,230
- Come out. - Hey, hurry and come out.

388
00:21:29,660 --> 00:21:33,330
- Hey. - I said come out.

389
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:35,730
- Come out. - Turtle Master, come out.

390
00:21:47,110 --> 00:21:49,610
(To CEO Baek Mi Young)

391
00:21:49,680 --> 00:21:52,850
Oh, right. This is an invitation to my party.

392
00:21:53,750 --> 00:21:55,190
Please make time to come,

393
00:21:55,190 --> 00:21:56,490
even if you have to clear your schedule.

394
00:21:59,990 --> 00:22:02,160
(To CEO Baek Mi Young)

395
00:22:04,330 --> 00:22:06,660
(Cheon Man Ju's Last Solo Party)

396
00:22:09,100 --> 00:22:11,270
(Location: Calvin Hotel, 6:00pm)

397
00:22:30,850 --> 00:22:32,160
Where were you?

398
00:22:32,320 --> 00:22:33,660
I waited for a long time.

399
00:22:34,060 --> 00:22:35,530
I told you not to come back.

400
00:22:35,760 --> 00:22:38,300
Why are you suddenly treating me like this?

401
00:22:38,800 --> 00:22:40,100
Don't do this to me.

402
00:22:40,460 --> 00:22:41,970
I told you, I'm getting married.

403
00:22:44,700 --> 00:22:46,870
What are you talking about all of a sudden?

404
00:22:47,400 --> 00:22:49,640
You know. I...

405
00:22:50,670 --> 00:22:53,080
I'm really all alone now.

406
00:22:53,710 --> 00:22:56,480
What am I supposed to do without you?

407
00:22:56,850 --> 00:22:57,910
She's pregnant.

408
00:23:00,420 --> 00:23:01,690
Three months along.

409
00:23:04,190 --> 00:23:06,120
I don't want to make you feel any more miserable.

410
00:23:50,300 --> 00:23:52,100
(To CEO Baek Mi Young)

411
00:23:54,910 --> 00:23:56,610
(To CEO Baek Mi Young)

412
00:24:05,350 --> 00:24:06,920
(Cheon Man Ju's Last Solo Party)

413
00:24:06,980 --> 00:24:08,690
(Location: Calvin Hotel, 6:00pm)

414
00:24:18,230 --> 00:24:19,930
Are we going to be here all night?

415
00:24:21,900 --> 00:24:24,500
You must have called me here because you have something to say.

416
00:24:29,640 --> 00:24:31,710
Jeez, this guy.

417
00:24:33,510 --> 00:24:34,740
Ji Won Ho.

418
00:24:37,310 --> 00:24:38,980
Ji Won Ho.

419
00:24:39,920 --> 00:24:42,290
Answer me, Ji Won Ho.

420
00:24:42,650 --> 00:24:44,150
Yes, I'm listening.

421
00:24:44,150 --> 00:24:45,490
Calvin Kim.

422
00:24:46,660 --> 00:24:47,960
My Mi Young.

423
00:24:49,460 --> 00:24:51,800
Can you make her happy?

424
00:24:53,430 --> 00:24:54,560
"My Mi Young?"

425
00:24:57,270 --> 00:24:58,470
Answer me.

426
00:24:59,040 --> 00:25:01,770
Tell me you'll make her happy!

427
00:25:02,370 --> 00:25:04,910
Gosh, I can't just hit a drunk guy.

428
00:25:13,750 --> 00:25:14,850
I...

429
00:25:15,420 --> 00:25:16,790
My Mi Young.

430
00:25:16,790 --> 00:25:18,490
Of course I'm going to make her happy.

431
00:25:18,860 --> 00:25:22,330
I will never hurt Mi Young the way you did.

432
00:25:23,330 --> 00:25:26,230
I'll make her so happy that she won't even remember...

433
00:25:26,300 --> 00:25:28,030
her time with you. I'll make sure of it.

434
00:25:28,630 --> 00:25:29,870
That promise.

435
00:25:30,530 --> 00:25:31,840
Never forget it.

436
00:25:34,340 --> 00:25:35,470
Because I...

437
00:25:36,540 --> 00:25:38,410
will never forget it either.

438
00:25:51,520 --> 00:25:52,590
(To CEO Baek Mi Young)

439
00:26:12,380 --> 00:26:13,680
(To CEO Baek Mi Young)

440
00:26:19,320 --> 00:26:21,280
You're going to Cheon Man Ju's party?

441
00:26:21,450 --> 00:26:22,890
Yes, I plan on going.

442
00:26:23,120 --> 00:26:24,960
But isn't it at Calvin Hotel?

443
00:26:25,420 --> 00:26:26,820
Are you sure you'll be okay?

444
00:26:27,960 --> 00:26:30,060
What do you mean, am I okay?

445
00:26:30,360 --> 00:26:31,760
Well,

446
00:26:31,930 --> 00:26:35,000
I'm just worried you might run into Calvin there.

447
00:26:35,070 --> 00:26:39,400
- I'm just worried. - It'd be a little awkward, I guess.

448
00:26:39,500 --> 00:26:41,740
But what can I do? It's all in the past.

449
00:26:42,470 --> 00:26:43,470
I guess so.

450
00:26:44,340 --> 00:26:45,580
Hey.

451
00:26:47,640 --> 00:26:49,680
Calvin got a divorce.

452
00:26:52,180 --> 00:26:53,220
A divorce?

453
00:26:53,620 --> 00:26:54,620
Yes.

454
00:26:55,320 --> 00:26:57,950
There was an article about it a while ago.

455
00:27:01,990 --> 00:27:02,990
Mi Young?

456
00:27:04,060 --> 00:27:05,060
Mi Young?

457
00:27:05,400 --> 00:27:09,270
Oh, here are some beads...

458
00:27:23,080 --> 00:27:24,310
What's wrong with that?

459
00:27:24,950 --> 00:27:27,250
You postponed your divorce because of Cheon Man Ju.

460
00:27:27,320 --> 00:27:30,020
So for her to go to a party Man Ju is throwing...

461
00:27:30,050 --> 00:27:31,090
is only natural, don't you think?

462
00:27:31,420 --> 00:27:33,790
Well, that's true. That's true, but...

463
00:27:34,790 --> 00:27:37,030
Of all places, the party is at...

464
00:27:39,460 --> 00:27:42,870
The party being at the Calvin Hotel is what's bothering you?

465
00:27:43,270 --> 00:27:45,900
Because it's obvious she'll run into Calvin there.

466
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:48,570
It's been a while since she broke up with Calvin.

467
00:27:49,310 --> 00:27:50,740
And that was before she met you.

468
00:27:50,840 --> 00:27:52,310
They only dated for a short while, right?

469
00:27:55,080 --> 00:27:56,080
What?

470
00:27:56,150 --> 00:27:57,810
Was it more serious?

471
00:27:59,280 --> 00:28:00,950
No, it's nothing like that.

472
00:28:01,250 --> 00:28:03,250
If not, what are you worried about?

473
00:28:03,550 --> 00:28:06,690
Besides, even if Calvin is divorced now,

474
00:28:07,060 --> 00:28:09,030
do you really think he'd hit on her?

475
00:28:09,290 --> 00:28:11,090
Not when you're by her side.

476
00:28:11,590 --> 00:28:12,760
He's divorced?

477
00:28:12,830 --> 00:28:13,830
You didn't know?

478
00:28:14,200 --> 00:28:15,500
When did he get divorced?

479
00:28:15,500 --> 00:28:17,100
Do you even live in this country?

480
00:28:18,300 --> 00:28:19,370
But then,

481
00:28:19,370 --> 00:28:20,640
you didn't even know who Cheon Man Ju was.

482
00:28:20,700 --> 00:28:21,970
Of course you wouldn't know.

483
00:28:24,740 --> 00:28:27,010
So that jerk Calvin got a divorce?

484
00:28:31,750 --> 00:28:32,820
Unbelievable.

485
00:28:42,390 --> 00:28:44,330
Are you happy with the bust length?

486
00:28:44,430 --> 00:28:46,430
Yes. If we add a tulle overlay here,

487
00:28:46,500 --> 00:28:48,400
it'll look more natural, elegant, and beautiful.

488
00:28:57,310 --> 00:28:59,580
Something with floral details like this would suit you too.

489
00:28:59,640 --> 00:29:02,180
This one, or if we put this on the front...

490
00:29:02,310 --> 00:29:04,650
Because it will draw the eyes away from the face.

491
00:29:04,710 --> 00:29:07,220
Will this line work? Now, as for the off-the-shoulder...

492
00:29:27,040 --> 00:29:30,540
Hi, everyone. Yes, hello.

493
00:29:31,370 --> 00:29:34,510
I have some really big news for you all today.

494
00:29:35,150 --> 00:29:37,380
Do you know who visited our shop?

495
00:29:38,480 --> 00:29:41,380
I should wait until we have over 300 viewers to tell you.

496
00:29:42,220 --> 00:29:43,220
We passed it.

497
00:29:44,020 --> 00:29:46,360
The person who visited our shop was...

498
00:29:46,420 --> 00:29:49,360
Drumroll, please. Cheon Man Ju.

499
00:29:50,630 --> 00:29:52,960
For her wedding dress,

500
00:29:53,030 --> 00:29:56,170
Cheon Man Ju chose our very own J&White.

501
00:29:56,230 --> 00:29:57,630
(J&White and Cheon Man Ju are a killer combination.)

502
00:29:57,900 --> 00:30:01,000
I'm so excited to see the dress Cheon Man Ju will be wearing.

503
00:30:01,240 --> 00:30:04,240
We're going to present a truly legendary dress,

504
00:30:04,340 --> 00:30:06,010
so please look forward to it.

505
00:30:06,080 --> 00:30:07,540
(Are you going to Cheon Man Ju's party today?)

506
00:30:07,610 --> 00:30:08,780
(CEO, are you going to the party?)

507
00:30:09,750 --> 00:30:11,480
Cheon Man Ju's party?

508
00:30:11,950 --> 00:30:13,950
(You have to tell us all about it. Can't wait for the pictures.)

509
00:30:14,120 --> 00:30:15,890
Of course. I have to go.

510
00:30:16,850 --> 00:30:17,990
Where do you think you're going?

511
00:30:18,250 --> 00:30:19,820
What kind of married woman just goes to a hotel?

512
00:30:19,890 --> 00:30:21,120
Are you out of your mind?

513
00:30:22,760 --> 00:30:24,460
My husband is so old-fashioned.

514
00:30:25,700 --> 00:30:26,860
Well then, I'll tell you all about it...

515
00:30:26,860 --> 00:30:29,330
when I'm back. He's not angry.

516
00:30:30,070 --> 00:30:31,470
What do you think you're doing?

517
00:30:31,530 --> 00:30:32,970
And you? Are you crazy?

518
00:30:33,040 --> 00:30:34,470
Thinking of going to the Calvin Hotel?

519
00:30:34,470 --> 00:30:35,710
What about the Calvin Hotel?

520
00:30:35,770 --> 00:30:37,310
What's wrong with going to the Calvin Hotel?

521
00:30:37,370 --> 00:30:39,940
Have you already forgotten what kind of person Calvin is?

522
00:30:40,110 --> 00:30:42,150
He cheated on you with another woman,

523
00:30:42,210 --> 00:30:43,880
got that other woman pregnant,

524
00:30:43,950 --> 00:30:45,550
and then married her.

525
00:30:45,950 --> 00:30:48,380
And Calvin recently got divorced.

526
00:30:48,450 --> 00:30:49,820
When I heard that jerk got divorced,

527
00:30:49,890 --> 00:30:51,250
why did I get such a bad feeling?

528
00:30:51,320 --> 00:30:53,620
- I just got a chill down my spine. - So what's your point?

529
00:30:53,690 --> 00:30:55,020
I said I'm going to the Calvin Hotel.

530
00:30:55,090 --> 00:30:56,990
Did I say I was going to a hotel with Calvin?

531
00:30:58,960 --> 00:31:01,100
Who knows? That jerk might approach you again.

532
00:31:01,160 --> 00:31:03,070
What if he tries to harm you?

533
00:31:03,130 --> 00:31:05,130
- What if? - Geez.

534
00:31:05,300 --> 00:31:06,570
What? Harm me?

535
00:31:07,070 --> 00:31:09,010
Isn't this a complete double standard?

536
00:31:09,510 --> 00:31:11,870
- Double standards? - Yes, double standards.

537
00:31:12,380 --> 00:31:14,980
Whatever harm Calvin could possibly do to me now,

538
00:31:14,980 --> 00:31:16,980
compared to how you've torn my heart out all this time,

539
00:31:17,050 --> 00:31:18,310
it would be a drop in the bucket.

540
00:31:18,510 --> 00:31:21,120
- Baek Mi Young. - Stop meddling in my business.

541
00:31:21,180 --> 00:31:22,890
Mind your own business.

542
00:31:27,620 --> 00:31:28,760
Darn it.

543
00:31:37,200 --> 00:31:38,330
Hello.

544
00:31:41,700 --> 00:31:44,710
- Little Dumplings. Hi. - Hi.

545
00:31:44,770 --> 00:31:48,140
You all know today's my party, right?

546
00:31:48,210 --> 00:31:49,380
(Today's dress is going to be legendary.)

547
00:31:49,450 --> 00:31:51,280
Stop telling me how pretty I am.

548
00:31:52,120 --> 00:31:53,120
In a few hours,

549
00:31:53,180 --> 00:31:55,620
this place is going to be completely packed.

550
00:31:55,950 --> 00:31:59,090
I'm just so excited.

551
00:32:00,220 --> 00:32:02,760
Oh, my. Ms. Lin Zhao Ming.

552
00:32:04,230 --> 00:32:07,500
Gosh, being invited to a party like this,

553
00:32:07,560 --> 00:32:10,500
I'm so happy I could die, don't you think?

554
00:32:26,050 --> 00:32:27,750
(Are you okay? This is insane.)

555
00:32:30,050 --> 00:32:33,820
Surprise. Were you surprised?

556
00:32:34,360 --> 00:32:36,990
I wanted to express with my whole body...

557
00:32:37,060 --> 00:32:39,900
that I'm so happy I could just fall over.

558
00:32:41,230 --> 00:32:44,530
Okay, my Little Dumplings. I'll see you all later.

559
00:32:45,000 --> 00:32:47,840
- Bye. - Bye.

560
00:32:47,970 --> 00:32:49,670
- Bye. - See you again.

561
00:32:51,210 --> 00:32:53,240
I'm so dumbfounded.

562
00:32:53,580 --> 00:32:55,650
I was in the middle of a live stream,

563
00:32:55,750 --> 00:32:57,580
and he just burst out of the room...

564
00:32:57,650 --> 00:32:59,450
and started yelling, "Are you crazy? Going to the Calvin Hotel?"

565
00:33:00,620 --> 00:33:02,590
He was just going completely ballistic.

566
00:33:02,750 --> 00:33:05,190
Seriously. I couldn't believe it.

567
00:33:05,250 --> 00:33:07,660
Is CEO Ji jealous or something?

568
00:33:07,720 --> 00:33:09,360
Jealous? Don't be ridiculous.

569
00:33:09,460 --> 00:33:11,330
It's like no matter what I do,

570
00:33:11,390 --> 00:33:13,300
he's just dying to sabotage it.

571
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:15,600
He's the absolute worst.

572
00:33:17,070 --> 00:33:18,070
Oh, yes.

573
00:33:19,400 --> 00:33:20,400
By the way,

574
00:33:20,400 --> 00:33:22,840
- what are you going to wear later? - What?

575
00:33:22,910 --> 00:33:23,910
I mean, Calvin...

576
00:33:25,270 --> 00:33:28,110
No. You're going to Cheon Man Ju's party.

577
00:33:28,180 --> 00:33:29,980
You can't just wear anything.

578
00:33:30,280 --> 00:33:32,780
Well, I have an outfit in mind.

579
00:33:33,050 --> 00:33:34,620
What? What are you going to wear?

580
00:33:34,980 --> 00:33:37,720
- Have you seen me in this before? - Let me see.

581
00:33:41,020 --> 00:33:42,190
No.

582
00:33:42,260 --> 00:33:45,630
- This is too plain. - You think so?

583
00:33:45,700 --> 00:33:46,830
Let's not do that.

584
00:33:46,900 --> 00:33:50,370
Since you're going, you should get all dressed up.

585
00:33:50,470 --> 00:33:52,900
You might run into Calvin.

586
00:33:52,970 --> 00:33:55,510
Just a minute ago, you were worried about me seeing Calvin.

587
00:33:55,570 --> 00:33:57,810
No, what I mean is,

588
00:33:57,870 --> 00:34:00,010
if you're going to run into him anyway,

589
00:34:00,080 --> 00:34:02,350
you should show up looking drop-dead gorgeous.

590
00:34:02,410 --> 00:34:03,550
That's what I'm saying.

591
00:34:04,010 --> 00:34:06,580
Make Calvin sick with regret for letting you go.

592
00:34:07,080 --> 00:34:08,080
What?

593
00:34:11,020 --> 00:34:13,160
Oh, give me a break.

594
00:34:13,660 --> 00:34:15,360
Is she the star of the party or something?

595
00:34:15,430 --> 00:34:17,590
Cheon Man Ju is the one getting married, not her.

596
00:34:17,990 --> 00:34:19,360
What's wrong, man?

597
00:34:20,130 --> 00:34:22,530
What, is she supposed to wear sweats to a party?

598
00:34:22,600 --> 00:34:24,030
What's wrong with sweats?

599
00:34:24,100 --> 00:34:25,470
She was invited because of work.

600
00:34:25,470 --> 00:34:27,170
She should just throw something on and go.

601
00:34:27,170 --> 00:34:28,300
Oh, come on.

602
00:34:28,840 --> 00:34:30,140
That's ridiculous.

603
00:34:30,640 --> 00:34:32,880
The more I think about it, the more pissed I get.

604
00:34:32,940 --> 00:34:34,480
Some of us are covered in thread,

605
00:34:34,540 --> 00:34:36,750
working ourselves to the bone, while others get all dolled up...

606
00:34:36,810 --> 00:34:38,480
and just think about going to a party.

607
00:34:40,420 --> 00:34:41,580
This isn't right.

608
00:34:42,690 --> 00:34:43,850
This really isn't right.

609
00:34:45,620 --> 00:34:46,620
Hey.

610
00:34:47,520 --> 00:34:48,720
Hey, where are you going?

611
00:34:48,960 --> 00:34:49,960
Hey.

612
00:34:51,460 --> 00:34:52,760
Oh, seriously.

613
00:34:55,470 --> 00:34:56,470
Oh my gosh.

614
00:34:58,900 --> 00:35:00,040
Oh my...

615
00:35:00,470 --> 00:35:03,470
You brought all the fabric from the shop.

616
00:35:04,910 --> 00:35:05,940
So,

617
00:35:06,610 --> 00:35:07,710
you're telling me...

618
00:35:07,780 --> 00:35:12,050
- to organise all of this today? - Yes. By colour and design,

619
00:35:12,110 --> 00:35:14,080
please organise and sort all of it.

620
00:35:14,420 --> 00:35:16,490
If you focus, it won't even take 3 or 4 hours.

621
00:35:16,550 --> 00:35:17,720
What? Three or four hours?

622
00:35:17,790 --> 00:35:18,920
I told you.

623
00:35:18,960 --> 00:35:20,660
I have plans tonight.

624
00:35:20,720 --> 00:35:22,690
Work comes before your evening plans.

625
00:35:22,690 --> 00:35:24,590
That's why I don't make plans,

626
00:35:24,690 --> 00:35:26,960
- so I can work. - Are you kidding me right now?

627
00:35:27,030 --> 00:35:28,130
So you're not going to work?

628
00:35:28,200 --> 00:35:29,470
Ji Won Ho, what is wrong with you?

629
00:35:29,470 --> 00:35:31,500
You just keep getting more and more petty.

630
00:35:31,570 --> 00:35:33,640
Petty? Are you done talking?

631
00:35:33,700 --> 00:35:35,270
No, I'm not done. What are you going to do about it?

632
00:35:35,340 --> 00:35:36,410
Go on. Say it.

633
00:35:36,470 --> 00:35:38,340
Hey, you're being petty and pathetic.

634
00:35:38,410 --> 00:35:39,840
I'm pathetic? Work first...

635
00:35:39,910 --> 00:35:42,510
- Is working hard pathetic? - You're disgusting.

636
00:35:42,580 --> 00:35:44,310
This is negligence of duty.

637
00:35:44,380 --> 00:35:45,780
Going to that party is work for me.

638
00:35:45,850 --> 00:35:47,320
You don't have time. Get to it.

639
00:35:47,680 --> 00:35:48,720
Hey, you...

640
00:35:52,720 --> 00:35:54,660
I guess you'd better work hard.

641
00:35:57,290 --> 00:35:58,290
Vice President Kang.

642
00:36:00,030 --> 00:36:02,160
Seriously, what's wrong with CEO Ji?

643
00:36:02,270 --> 00:36:03,530
What about CEO Ji?

644
00:36:03,700 --> 00:36:06,500
He just dropped a bombshell on Mi Young.

645
00:36:06,570 --> 00:36:07,570
A work bombshell.

646
00:36:07,740 --> 00:36:09,770
I mean, she's going to Cheon Man Ju's party today.

647
00:36:09,840 --> 00:36:11,510
And he knows that perfectly well.

648
00:36:11,610 --> 00:36:13,740
I mean, he's treating her like Cinderella or something.

649
00:36:14,240 --> 00:36:17,080
Don't you think CEO Ji is being way too spiteful?

650
00:36:17,180 --> 00:36:19,820
I completely understand where CEO Ji is coming from.

651
00:36:20,320 --> 00:36:22,180
- What? - If it were me,

652
00:36:22,250 --> 00:36:23,550
putting everything else aside,

653
00:36:23,620 --> 00:36:25,620
the name of the party venue alone would upset me.

654
00:36:26,490 --> 00:36:27,790
For example, Director Song,

655
00:36:28,320 --> 00:36:31,460
if your ex-husband's name was plastered all over a hotel...

656
00:36:31,530 --> 00:36:33,900
What does my ex-husband have to do with this?

657
00:36:34,460 --> 00:36:35,460
Pardon?

658
00:36:36,730 --> 00:36:39,040
There's zero chance of that happening.

659
00:36:39,800 --> 00:36:42,540
Who would name a hotel the Bong Gu Hotel?

660
00:36:49,610 --> 00:36:51,050
Her ex-husband's name is Bong Gu?

661
00:36:52,680 --> 00:36:55,250
I'm sorry, Director Song.

662
00:38:07,060 --> 00:38:08,190
What are you doing, you jerk?

663
00:38:12,830 --> 00:38:14,000
That scared me.

664
00:38:15,670 --> 00:38:17,300
What a messed-up dream that was.

665
00:38:18,870 --> 00:38:20,400
I need to get it together.

666
00:38:55,970 --> 00:38:56,970
Glad you could make it.

667
00:38:58,140 --> 00:38:59,140
Is everything delicious?

668
00:39:06,620 --> 00:39:07,620
It's a pleasure.

669
00:39:08,180 --> 00:39:09,190
Hello.

670
00:39:09,450 --> 00:39:11,220
Oh my, you're here.

671
00:39:15,960 --> 00:39:17,690
This is my fiancé.

672
00:39:19,530 --> 00:39:21,160
Hello. It's a pleasure to meet you.

673
00:39:21,300 --> 00:39:23,370
Yes, my sincerest congratulations on your marriage.

674
00:39:23,570 --> 00:39:25,070
I hope I didn't put you in an awkward position...

675
00:39:25,130 --> 00:39:26,140
by asking you to come.

676
00:39:26,600 --> 00:39:28,170
Not at all. Of course I had to come.

677
00:39:35,680 --> 00:39:36,780
Are you...

678
00:39:37,650 --> 00:39:39,420
looking for someone?

679
00:39:39,720 --> 00:39:41,220
Not at all. No.

680
00:39:42,050 --> 00:39:43,390
Well, then, please enjoy yourself.

681
00:39:44,090 --> 00:39:46,420
- Okay. - Shall we go upstairs?

682
00:39:59,170 --> 00:40:00,840
Hi there, my Little Dumplings.

683
00:40:01,840 --> 00:40:04,640
Okay, this is where I'm having my pre-wedding party.

684
00:40:04,840 --> 00:40:06,840
What do you think of the party decorations?

685
00:40:07,480 --> 00:40:08,840
Isn't it so pretty?

686
00:40:09,410 --> 00:40:11,450
What? You think I'm prettier?

687
00:40:12,450 --> 00:40:13,550
(Cheon Man Ju has the best taste.)

688
00:40:13,650 --> 00:40:15,150
Ta-da.

689
00:40:15,850 --> 00:40:18,450
What do you think of my dress? It's so pretty, right?

690
00:40:19,960 --> 00:40:21,190
But you know what?

691
00:40:21,690 --> 00:40:23,930
The dress I'll be wearing on my wedding day...

692
00:40:23,990 --> 00:40:25,590
is even prettier than this one.

693
00:40:25,660 --> 00:40:26,730
(We want to see the dress.)

694
00:40:26,800 --> 00:40:27,960
(Show us the dress.)

695
00:40:28,160 --> 00:40:29,470
You want to see it now?

696
00:40:31,000 --> 00:40:32,000
Hold on.

697
00:40:37,370 --> 00:40:40,340
Darn it. This is so distracting, I can't work.

698
00:40:45,880 --> 00:40:47,220
CEO Ji.

699
00:40:48,120 --> 00:40:49,520
This is Man Ju.

700
00:40:51,120 --> 00:40:52,420
Yes, Ms. Man Ju.

701
00:40:52,790 --> 00:40:55,490
Is Man Ju's dress finished?

702
00:40:55,960 --> 00:40:56,960
The dress?

703
00:40:58,460 --> 00:41:00,600
Yes, the dress is finished. Why?

704
00:41:02,700 --> 00:41:05,500
Well, I want to try it on soon today.

705
00:41:06,400 --> 00:41:08,300
Quickly.

706
00:41:09,100 --> 00:41:11,340
You want to try on the dress today?

707
00:41:11,870 --> 00:41:14,410
Yes, right now.

708
00:41:14,810 --> 00:41:16,050
Right now?

709
00:41:16,350 --> 00:41:17,350
Yes.

710
00:41:19,380 --> 00:41:22,150
(Cheon Man Ju's Last Solo Party, Location: Calvin Hotel, 6:00pm)

711
00:42:03,360 --> 00:42:04,360
Please just go.

712
00:42:05,530 --> 00:42:07,430
I don't want to make you feel any more miserable.

713
00:42:22,680 --> 00:42:23,680
Mi Young.

714
00:42:28,650 --> 00:42:30,350
Yes. It's been a while.

715
00:42:32,920 --> 00:42:33,990
It really has been a long time.

716
00:42:49,910 --> 00:42:51,610
Delivery for someone here?

717
00:42:56,310 --> 00:42:58,680
Oh, there you are.

718
00:42:59,580 --> 00:43:01,780
Well, long time no see, Mr. Calvin.

719
00:43:07,390 --> 00:43:08,460
He looks scared.

720
00:43:09,990 --> 00:43:11,190
Nothing happened, right?

721
00:43:11,590 --> 00:43:12,630
What do you mean?

722
00:43:13,200 --> 00:43:14,200
Never mind.

723
00:43:14,600 --> 00:43:16,700
Not that it could've happened. Not with so many people watching.

724
00:43:18,130 --> 00:43:19,470
What are you doing here all of a sudden?

725
00:43:19,770 --> 00:43:21,640
- Well... - I ordered it.

726
00:43:24,310 --> 00:43:25,310
Hello.

727
00:43:26,410 --> 00:43:28,080
I had to try on my dress today,

728
00:43:28,140 --> 00:43:29,850
so I pestered CEO Ji about it.

729
00:43:31,010 --> 00:43:32,010
Right now?

730
00:43:32,920 --> 00:43:35,050
That was some fast delivery.

731
00:43:36,250 --> 00:43:37,690
I guess you ride a motorcycle.

732
00:43:38,020 --> 00:43:40,960
Yes. Speed and accuracy are the lifeblood of delivery.

733
00:43:41,390 --> 00:43:43,830
Here you are. Perfectly prepared, just as you ordered.

734
00:43:43,890 --> 00:43:45,490
The special finishing touch is a gift from me.

735
00:43:45,790 --> 00:43:47,900
Oh, I'm so excited.

736
00:43:48,630 --> 00:43:50,570
- Let's go. - What?

737
00:43:50,630 --> 00:43:52,570
Let's go quickly.

738
00:43:53,200 --> 00:43:54,200
Wait...

739
00:44:08,520 --> 00:44:11,120
Can we talk for a minute?

740
00:44:15,120 --> 00:44:16,760
Man Ju, are you almost ready?

741
00:44:17,060 --> 00:44:18,490
I'm ready.

742
00:44:20,030 --> 00:44:21,500
Ta-da.

743
00:44:23,470 --> 00:44:26,370
- What do you think? - It looks amazing on you.

744
00:44:26,540 --> 00:44:27,540
I like it.

745
00:44:28,070 --> 00:44:30,770
But I think the waistline could be more defined.

746
00:44:31,010 --> 00:44:32,370
Something's just not quite right.

747
00:44:32,610 --> 00:44:33,640
But did you not see it?

748
00:44:33,640 --> 00:44:35,480
The special finishing touch I prepared?

749
00:44:35,740 --> 00:44:37,450
Wait a minute.

750
00:44:37,450 --> 00:44:39,480
A finishing touch? There's a finishing touch?

751
00:44:40,280 --> 00:44:41,350
Sure.

752
00:44:48,520 --> 00:44:50,860
- I found it. - That, yes, that's it.

753
00:44:50,930 --> 00:44:52,360
Oh, so this is it. Quick, put it on me.

754
00:44:52,360 --> 00:44:53,530
Okay, I got it.

755
00:44:59,900 --> 00:45:01,100
Hold on, I will do it.

756
00:45:08,780 --> 00:45:10,410
As tight as possible.

757
00:45:11,810 --> 00:45:13,620
There we go.

758
00:45:18,850 --> 00:45:20,720
It's so beautiful.

759
00:45:21,060 --> 00:45:22,320
I'm going to go show this off.

760
00:45:28,600 --> 00:45:29,600
What did you want to say?

761
00:45:30,330 --> 00:45:31,770
The invitation you got from Man Ju.

762
00:45:32,670 --> 00:45:33,670
I was the one who sent it.

763
00:45:34,240 --> 00:45:36,240
You did?

764
00:45:36,970 --> 00:45:37,970
Why?

765
00:45:38,610 --> 00:45:39,610
Because I missed you.

766
00:45:41,810 --> 00:45:42,980
I have really missed you.

767
00:45:44,610 --> 00:45:48,150
You missed me.

768
00:45:51,490 --> 00:45:52,550
So what?

769
00:45:53,990 --> 00:45:57,290
What's going to change just by us looking at each other?

770
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:01,000
Look,

771
00:46:01,900 --> 00:46:03,930
from now on, just pretend you don't know me.

772
00:46:05,130 --> 00:46:06,140
To me,

773
00:46:06,870 --> 00:46:09,200
you are like someone who doesn't exist.

774
00:46:12,610 --> 00:46:13,710
I'm going to go now.

775
00:46:15,510 --> 00:46:16,510
Are you happy?

776
00:46:19,380 --> 00:46:20,380
Are you?

777
00:46:25,520 --> 00:46:26,560
Of course.

778
00:46:27,690 --> 00:46:28,960
You saw my husband, didn't you?

779
00:46:30,190 --> 00:46:31,190
I'm...

780
00:46:32,900 --> 00:46:34,230
doing very well.

781
00:46:35,600 --> 00:46:36,770
I'm incredibly happy.

782
00:46:47,640 --> 00:46:48,640
CEO Ji.

783
00:46:50,050 --> 00:46:51,650
You don't recognise me?

784
00:46:52,210 --> 00:46:53,220
What?

785
00:46:54,950 --> 00:46:56,120
Take a closer look.

786
00:46:58,820 --> 00:46:59,890
Don't you remember me?

787
00:47:07,300 --> 00:47:08,460
Are you hitting on me?

788
00:47:10,100 --> 00:47:11,100
What?

789
00:47:12,000 --> 00:47:13,240
That's strange.

790
00:47:13,500 --> 00:47:16,070
You look so young. Why are you using such an old-fashioned pickup line?

791
00:47:17,310 --> 00:47:20,580
Look, I'm sorry, but you're not my type at all.

792
00:47:21,640 --> 00:47:24,410
- What? - Stop playing games.

793
00:47:26,180 --> 00:47:28,580
And I'm only saying this because you remind me of my little sister,

794
00:47:29,220 --> 00:47:30,820
but you shouldn't mess with a married man.

795
00:47:30,890 --> 00:47:32,120
You could get into real trouble.

796
00:47:33,390 --> 00:47:34,390
Milan.

797
00:47:36,360 --> 00:47:38,560
- What? - Don't you remember?

798
00:47:39,360 --> 00:47:42,300
Eight years ago, in Milan.

799
00:47:44,530 --> 00:47:45,530
Milan?

800
00:47:55,010 --> 00:47:56,110
If we look at these models,

801
00:47:56,180 --> 00:47:58,580
accessories from the new collection would really make them stand out.

802
00:47:58,650 --> 00:48:01,950
Yes, I agree. The material and the design...

803
00:48:02,020 --> 00:48:04,290
are both important. What do you think?

804
00:48:04,350 --> 00:48:06,320
- I completely agree. - Thank you.

805
00:48:06,420 --> 00:48:07,720
Excuse me, I'm just going to use the restroom.

806
00:48:07,820 --> 00:48:08,820
Of course, go ahead.

807
00:48:22,170 --> 00:48:23,670
Where do you think you're going?

808
00:48:36,320 --> 00:48:38,720
Excuse me, you're Korean, right?

809
00:48:43,860 --> 00:48:44,860
I remember now.

810
00:48:45,290 --> 00:48:48,700
That kid from Milan. No, the pickpocket.

811
